  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "From ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/~cwilper/2010/03/18/Authentication+Challenge+Control+-+A+Thought+Experiment"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/~cwilper/2010/03/18/Authentication+Challenge+Control+-+A+Thought+Experiment",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Fedora's SOAP API has historically been split into two: API-A and API-M. The REST API, being resource-oriented, naturally isn't. And the control over which endpoints can be set to require authentication is inconsistent across the two. The old \"Authenticate for API-A? Authenticate for API-M?\" options no longer make sense when you look at Fedora's APIs as a whole.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Here's one way the situation could be improved.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1. For the SOAP API (all read-oriented and write-oriented methods), always require authentication.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2. For the REST API, on a per-verb basis (POST/PUT/DELETE/GET), offer the following options at install time:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "1. Proactive Challenge: Always require authentication.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2. Reactive Challenge: Only require authentication if an un-authenticated request failed due to AuthZ rules.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
